 cavity  there are metal clips  Further sectioning through the specimen reveals predominantly fibrous tissue admixed with small amount of fatty tissue  There is a 0 4cm clear fluid filled cyst otherwise no other regions are grossly appreciated or palpated  Representative sections are submitted  Section code  A B  Biopsy cavity entirely submitted C  Soft fibrous tissue adjacent laterally to biopsy site  D  Firm fibrous tissue adjacent medially to biopsy site  E  Additional section of firm fibrotic area  F  Additional section of soft fibrous tissue  G  Section to include overlying skin and nipple areolar complex  H  Cyst I  Overlying skin with scar Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  abdominal flap  are four irregular portions of subcutaneous tissue  Three of the portions have overlying tan white skin  The specimen aggregates REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  Sectioning through the specimen reveals unremarkable subcutaneous tissue  A representative section is submitted in cassette J  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  SOFT TISSUE  ABDOMINAL WALL FLAP    report_end  , Unknown.
